foreign  in the 1953 science fiction film the  beast from 20 000 fathoms a giant  monster attacks New York City as giant  monsters are known to do  while the film's plot isn't particularly  noteworthy one element that stands out  comes about halfway through the film  when a group of scientists try to figure  out the evolutionary history of the  mysterious creature our interest in the  theoretical biology of unknown life  forms hasn't gone anywhere for the past  Century stories of Cryptids like Bigfoot  or the Loch Ness monster have continued  to Fascinate and while these creatures  likely don't exist that doesn't mean it  isn't Fun to speculate on their biology  enter cryptism logicon a book that  imagines evolutionary backstories for  legendary creatures created by renowned  paleontologist Darren Nash alongside  Channel Mainstays cm kosman and John  Conway the volume is so detailed that I  had to know more  so where did the idea of writing a book  on the speculative biology of Cryptids  come from  the idea did originate with me I said  well there's all these creatures in  cryptos orgy that are posited as  potentially real animals but are  essentially exercises in speculative  zoology the cryptozoological literature  has got this extraordinary amount of  speculation about if these creatures are  real what are they like what's their  evolutionary history  so for this entry into the archive we'll  investigate the imagined biology of the  world's most famous Cryptids and you can  purchase the book and follow and support  the creators using links in the  description below now let's explore the  creatures of crypto zoologicon  we'll start with the celebrities of the  Cryptid World The Hairy humanoids best  known for their alleged footprints  the most familiar Cryptids are Bigfoot  Yeti every culture in the world that we  know about has Legends of wild people of  some kind I think it's a good case to be  made that that's a human-wide  expectation I think it's already  embedded within our cultural landscape  Bigfoot in the yeti may be a  socio-cultural phenomenon rather than an  Undiscovered primate species but if we  were to Envision their evolutionary  history an interesting challenge emerges  just how do these speculative hominids  relate to us and to each other the  crypto zoologicon team solution is to  imagine Bigfoot in the yeti as large  herbivorous Eeps more closely related to  orangutans than humans the project  imagines the yeti in Bigfoot to be close  cousins related subspecies possessing  different adaptations for their  respective environments in fact the  crypto zoologicon team created an entire  phylogenetic tree to show how these  lineages connect not just to each other  but to other lesser-known ape Cryptids  from around the world the orang pen deck  for example are smaller red-coated  humanoids from Sumatran folklore which  the team pictures as another member of  this forgotten branch of the primate  family tree but this is just scratching  the surface of the team's creativity  another famous yet far more unusual  Cryptid comes from the folklore of the  Americas the chupacabra is a fabled  creature said to drain the blood from  livestock like goats what exactly the  chupacabra is supposed to look like  varies a lot between alleged eyewitness  descriptions from a dog-like creature to  more of a bloodthirsty kangaroo  if the chupacabra were a real animal the  team imagines it would be a semi-bipedal  nocturnal Predator yet unexpectedly the  team pictures the chupacabra is a giant  relative of the opossum the opossum  lineage might not seem like the one most  likely to produce a bloodthirsty Terror  of the night but in fact the strong jaws  and formidable upper canines of opossums  would require little evolutionary  modification to produce a large-bodied  predator  if such a creature did roam the Americas  one would have to be extra careful after  the sun went down  when we think about reptilian beasts  lurking below 