ian marsupial of which there are  several other theories suggest that the  bunyip actually comes from sightings of  animals like the Platypus which frankly  does look quite a bit like a mythical  creature but if the bunyip were an  Undiscovered animal the team's concept  for the creature is a semi-aquatic  marsupial the idea of an aquatic  marsupial presents an interesting  challenge as marsupials give birth to  underdeveloped babies that they raise in  a pouch as a solution the the team  proposes that like the unusual South  American Water possum the bunyip's pouch  has a watertight seal such an adaptation  could allow the bunyip to thrive in  aquatic environments something that real  Australian marsupials have struggled to  do  the tale of the Beast of javudon is one  of the most genuinely interesting and  intriguing of cryptozoological mysteries  between 1764 and 1767 in Southeastern  France over 70 people seemingly perished  from encounters with an enormous  wolf-like Beast the Beast quickly became  legendary in multiple large wolves  believed to be responsible for the  beast's attacks were slain during that  time allegedly a rogue hyena was  eventually caught and killed as well as  unlikely as that might sound the  animal's pelt was documented going on  display in Paris years later confirming  that an escaped hyena really did briefly  roam the French Countryside in view of  all this it seems the attacks came from  numerous culprits the stories of which  were inadvertently combined to form the  legend but now let's imagine that the  Beast of javudon was a sing single  undocumented monster taking inspiration  from reports that the Beast had curved  claws in a long slender tail the team  interprets the creature not as a wolf or  hyena but a type of giant mustelid  mustolids are a family of carnivorous  mammals that includes otters ferrets and  Wolverines this version of the Beast of  javudon would be an entirely new subset  of the mustelid family and would make  the European Countryside far more  dangerous  thanks in part to a somewhat notorious  faux documentary that aired on the  Discovery Channel in 2013. the idea that  a certain bus size prehistoric shark  could still be living undetected has  become a popular one  given your expertise as a paleontologist  just how outlandish is it that the  Megalodon survived into the modern era  there's no chance that it's still alive  it's not really appreciated how poor the  case is lots of data on the position of  Megalodon teeth in the fossil record has  shown that this shark did not survive  into the Holocene the modern era and it  probably didn't even definitely solve  into the pleistocene most of them have  turned out to be older than about two  million years old way way way before the  the modern era yet in a speculative  parallel universe where the Megalodon  did still swim in the Seas what would it  look like in order for a whale eating  shark to remain elusive it would likely  have to have evolved into a deep water  fish that lurks in undersea Canyons the  team suggests that this new Abyssal  Megalodon would be a ghostly white and  would be a separate species from its  pliocene ancestors such Terrors of the  deep would certainly make swimming more  nerve-wracking  on the Indonesian island of java a demon  is said to fly through the mountains on  leathery Wings infrequent reports from  the 1920s describe the ahuel a bat-like  terror with a massive wingspan in the  face of a primate while it's unlikely  such an organism ever existed the  concept of a giant bat monster isn't too  hard to reimagine as something more  biologically plausible the team  envisions the ahul as an unknown bat  lineage even larger than the fox face  Mega bats a Burly Predator the Hool is  able to walk bipedally on the ground  bringing prey to the forest floor after  tackling them in the air in aggressive  carnivore this creature possesses a  short snout that vaguely resembles the  face of a monkey all in all it's an  astute reimagining of a rather unlikely  life form  according to Folklore hidden deep in the  misty Moors of Scotland lurks a spectral  horse kilpie is an old Scottish name for  an equine monster said to dwell within  deep Lakes hoping to drag unsuspecting  travelers to a watery grave since horses  aren't amphibious the Kelpie is a  challenging creature to reimagine as a  plausible life form but there are  several hoofed mammal species like  wildebeest or water buffalo that do  routinely wallow in rivers and lakes  more surprisingly there are even some  species of chevrotain bizarre animals  also known as mouse deer that are known  to walk underwater along the bottom of  pools so the team imagines the Kelpie as  giant relatives of the Chevrolet that  possess thick manes and cloven hooves  that make them look superficially  horse-like from a distance reimagining  Kelpies as semi-aquatic chevertains  could also explain their occasional  carnivorous behavior from the Legends as  shiv retains or omnivores the team  imagines the Kelpie possess fang-like  teeth to drag prey into the water which  would on occasion include humans  in the Lee koala River Region of the  Congo Basin a reptile-like creature with  plates on its back supposedly lurks and  the swamp upon hearing of this  creature's description some Outsiders  interpreted the beast called the mumbilu  membilu membilu as some kind of aquatic  stegosaur that had miraculously survived  the KT Extinction event while this would  be cool it's quite the leap to make and  even very speculative reimagining the  team found the stegosaur explanation to  be too far-fetched  if you're gonna take seriously the idea  this is a real animal then stegosaurus  you know way down the list of things you  could class as probable and so four  cryptos or Lodge gone we thought wait a  minute there's this group of relatively  large tropical African fish that have  some amphibious capability and have  dorsal finlets uh forming 