s flap sealing the tail in  place the western United States would  certainly be more perilous if deadly  snakes could roll around at high speeds  but I still find myself wishing I lived  in a world with hoop snakes  foreign but according to Darren Nash  himself just because a creature likely  doesn't exist it doesn't mean it can't  tell us something about ourselves and  our cultures I think Krypton has an  enormous potential to teach us a lot  about how we behave people have these  particular kinds of creatures as sort of  fixtures of the imagination you go to a  big deep Cold Lake you look in the water  there's automatically the idea even if  you see absolutely nothing there's the  idea that there could be some giant  scary and predatory monster in the lake  that is a that's like a fixture of our  culture our species as a whole we often  seem to have the same kind of creatures  uh for me it's like cryptos orgy is is  uh is culture is like firmly embedded  within cultures whether those creatures  exist or not  a tremendous thank you to Darren Nash  for speaking to me about cryptozoology  once again you can purchase cryptozo  logicon to see more reimagined Cryptids  and follow and support the creators  using the links in the description below  and as always thanks for watching if you  enjoyed this entry please lend your  support by liking subscribing and  hitting the notification icon to stay up  to date on all things curious see you in  the next video  foreign

